  "articleBody": "Adding a room to your home is a big project, and getting the framing right is super important. There are a few common mistakes folks make that can really mess things up down the line. For starters, never jump the gun and begin framing before all your permits and approvals are firmly in hand. It sounds obvious, but it happens, and it can lead to costly rework or even demolition. Another big one is not fully considering how the new framing will integrate with your existing structure. You can't just build a box next to your house; it needs to connect seamlessly, otherwise you're looking at structural issues and energy leaks. Finally, don't overlook whether your project needs a structural engineer. If your addition changes load paths or is complex, an engineer's review is crucial. If you're ever unsure about these steps, especially when dealing with structural connections or inspections, it's always smart to bring in a professional. They've got the experience to make sure your room addition framing is solid and safe.",
